# A screw thread as one row of the group list (an extension): its four
# groups fold under the thread, [+] shows them and [-] folds them again;
# the row's arrows move the thread as one, or say why not; its box hides
# all four; its name opens the thread's screen, which suppresses the
# thread whole and deletes it in one step, which undo brings back.
key c
move 300 300
down L 300 300
up L 300 300
move 350 300
down L 350 300
up L 350 300
key esc
key x shift
move 350 300
down L 350 300
up L 350 300
menu Features|Screw Thread...
twmove 172 110
twdown L 172 110
twup L 172 110
edit M6x1
twmove 220 150
twdown L 220 150
twup L 220 150
edit 9
twmove 181 190
twdown L 181 190
twup L 181 190
twmove 60 230
twdown L 60 230
twup L 60 230
twmove 37 260
twdown L 37 260
twup L 37 260
tw
# Home: the thread's four groups are one row.
twmove 28 10
twdown L 28 10
twup L 28 10
tw
dump
# [+] shows the thread's groups under its row, [-] folds them.
twmove 507 180
twdown L 507 180
twup L 507 180
tw
twmove 507 180
twdown L 507 180
twup L 507 180
tw
# Up: refused, the blank is drawn on the extrusion's circle; down: last.
answer ok
twmove 543 180
twdown L 543 180
twup L 543 180
answer ok
twmove 561 180
twdown L 561 180
twup L 561 180
# The box hides all four groups; undo shows them again.
twmove 62 180
twdown L 62 180
twup L 62 180
dump
key z ctrl
dump
# The thread's name opens its screen.
twmove 200 180
twdown L 200 180
twup L 200 180
tw
# Suppress the thread whole: home says so; then bring it back.
twmove 462 170
twdown L 462 170
twup L 462 170
tw
dump
twmove 28 10
twdown L 28 10
twup L 28 10
tw
twmove 200 180
twdown L 200 180
twup L 200 180
tw
